/target/
**/target/
**/.slopium/
# The fixture the Nix bridge builds is not somebody's local configuration: its
# index path and trusted key are what `checks.lock-build` resolves against, so a
# clone without them cannot run the check.
!/tests/consumer/.slopium/
/.notes/
*.o
*.s
# `*.s` above is emitted assembly, which is build output wherever it appears. A
# fixture's entry stub is the opposite: hand-written source that `c-sources`
# hands to `cc`, and the freestanding fixture is nothing without it.
!/tests/projects/**/*.s
*.out
nvim.log
/tests/projects/**/Slopium.lock
/examples/**/Slopium.lock
